{
  "schema": 1,
  "name": "Warcraft Reborn Prestige works like Conquest of Azeroth's and also resets the active talent spec and Mystic Enchant preset",
  "contract": [
    "Issue 8326: Chromie refused stock classes on Warcraft Reborn (Prestige Mode is only available to Conquest of Azeroth classes).",
    "A Reborn character at the Prestige level activates Prestige like a CoA class: level 1, 0 experience, the Prestige aura, the rewards, the quest reset and the racial start.",
    "The active specialization's talents (its free-pick build) are reset, every Mystic Enchant in the active preset is removed, class spells above level 1 are forgotten and a lower rank becomes usable again.",
    "The specialization is the specialization slot (swap spells 979993 and on, as for a free-pick Hero): activating another slot is refused until the Prestige level, then allowed.",
    "The Prestige level is the realm's level cap (MaxPlayerLevel, 80 as shipped), so the character starts at 80 and completes the cycle by reaching 80 again."
  ],
  "timeout_ms": 240000,
  "location": {
    "map": 0,
    "x": -8816.5,
    "y": 627.0,
    "z": 94.1,
    "o": 3.8
  },
